          <a href="#rights" class="toc-link">6. Your Privacy Rights</a>
        </nav>
      </aside>

      <main class="legal-content">
        <section id="introduction" class="legal-section">
          <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
          <p>At FlynnBot ("we," "us," or "our"), we take your privacy seriously. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal information when you use our bot and dashboard services.</p>
          <p>We handle your data in accordance with the <strong>Privacy Act 1988 (Cth)</strong> and the <strong>Australian Privacy Principles (APPs)</strong>, alongside consideration for data protection regulations applicable within the Northern Territory, Australia.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="collection" class="legal-section">
          <h2>2. Data We Collect</h2>
          <p>We limit the information we collect to what is necessary for FlynnBot to function optimally within your Discord community:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>User & Guild Identifying Information:</strong> We store Discord IDs representing users, text channels, roles, and guilds.</li>
            <li><strong>Dashboard Analytics:</strong> For users accessing our dashboard, we may collect basic IP addresses and session information to prevent abuse and manage authenticated sessions.</li>
            <li><strong>Message Contents:</strong> FlynnBot only stores message contents temporarily (in memory) for the purpose of the Automod filtering and short-term message logging or sniping. Persistent message logs are sent directly to the designated channel in your Discord server, reducing our storage footprint.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="usage" class="legal-section">
          <h2>3. How We Use Your Data</h2>
          <p>The information described above is used strictly for technical performance and the provision of our Service. Specifically:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>To enforce moderation routines configured by the server administration (e.g., warnings, kicks, bans).</li>
            <li>To track user leveling, experience points, and economy balances configured per server.</li>
            <li>To manage dashboard access using Discord OAuth2 authentication.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Under no circumstances will FlynnBot sell, rent, or lease your personal information to third parties.</strong></p>
        </section>

        <section id="retention" class="legal-section">
          <h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
          <p>We keep your personal information only for as long as needed to fulfill the purposes for which it was collected:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Server configurations and logs are maintained while FlynnBot remains a member of your Discord server.</li>
            <li>Once FlynnBot is removed or a server deletion request is made, we routinely purge related records from our database to comply with minimum data retention guidelines.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="disclosure" class="legal-section">
          <h2>5. Disclosure & Cross-Border Transfers</h2>
          <p>FlynnBot's infrastructure is hosted on secure cloud providers. Because Discord operates globally, displaying information in your Discord server may result in cross-border data transit. We do not disclose your personal information externally, except:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>When required by law enforcement or a valid court order from within the Northern Territory or broader Australian jurisdiction.</li>
            <li>To essential service providers (such as hosting infrastructure) bound by strict confidentiality and data protection agreements.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="rights" class="legal-section">
          <h2>6. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
          <p>Under the APPs, you have the right to request access to the personal information we hold about you and request corrections if it is inaccurate. Because FlynnBot operates via Discord, the majority of your user data relies directly on your Discord profile.</p>
          <div class="legal-box">
            <h4>Data Deletion Requests</h4>
            <p>If you wish to have your data purged from FlynnBot's systems, server owners can simply kick the bot from their server. To request a manual deletion or inquire about your data under Australian Privacy laws, please reach out via our official <a href="#">Support Server</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>
    </div>
